cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "ThreatDiff: Threat models generated from agent configuration, checked on every pull request"
abstract: >-
  ThreatDiff builds a capability graph from an AI agent's configuration
  (system prompt, tools, MCP servers, data sources and triggers), finds paths
  from untrusted input to dangerous actions, and reports the paths each pull
  request opens or closes, labelled with OWASP and MITRE ATLAS identifiers.
authors:
  - family-names: Sadayamuthu
    given-names: Karthikeyan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3539-6048"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sadayamuthu/threatdiff"
url: "https://openastra.org"
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - threat modeling
  - MCP
  - OWASP
  - MITRE ATLAS
  - CI
